[Resource](class_resource.html#class-resource) **preload**(path: [String](class_string.html#class-string)) [🔗](#class-gdscript-method-preload)

Returns a [Resource](class_resource.html#class-resource) from the filesystem located at `path`. During run-time, the resource is loaded when the script is being parsed. This function effectively acts as a reference to that resource. Note that this function requires `path` to be a constant [String](class_string.html#class-string). If you want to load a resource from a dynamic/variable path, use [load()](#class-gdscript-method-load).

**Note:** Resource paths can be obtained by right-clicking on a resource in the Assets Panel and choosing "Copy Path", or by dragging the file from the FileSystem dock into the current script.

